    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκατά-ληπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to apprehend</i> or
				<i>recognize</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
				<u>Praef.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.28.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				1.1a
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔχειν</span> to be <i>easily bandaged by</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάληψις</span> (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>easy to capture</i>, of cities, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατειχίζειν</span>
			.</div>
